\DOC MAYCHANGE_STATE_UPDATE_TAC

\TYPE {MAYCHANGE_STATE_UPDATE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Replaces the goal's accumulated {MAYCHANGE} frame assumption, which relates the
initial state to one state, by an updated frame relating the initial state to
the successor state named in the goal's state-update equation, extending the
frame with any components written by that update.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. It acts only on the assumptions, leaving the conclusion
unchanged and producing a single subgoal. The unique assumption of the form
{(MAYCHANGE ... ,, ...) s t} (possibly a bare {MAYCHANGE []} relation) is
deleted, and an assumption of the same shape is appended at the end of the
assumption list: the second state becomes the later state {u} occurring in the
goal's {write ... = u} premise, and zero or more further {MAYCHANGE [...]}
components are composed on the right, in order, for those state components the
write touches that are not already listed (if all written components are
already covered, the component list is unchanged). All other assumptions keep
their order, so those after the removed one shift index.
{
     A, (MAYCHANGE [c1] ,, ... ,, MAYCHANGE [cn]) s t ?- t'
     ===================================================================================  MAYCHANGE_STATE_UPDATE_TAC
     A, (MAYCHANGE [c1] ,, ... ,, MAYCHANGE [cn] ,, MAYCHANGE [d1] ,, ... ,, MAYCHANGE [dk]) s u ?- t'
}
\noindent where k may be zero.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of outcome, always on goals
whose conclusion is an implication from a state-update equation to an
{eventually} statement carrying a {MAYCHANGE} frame.

\ENDDOC
